    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57-a2">

                <pb facs="0185" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg93"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Foreign Affairs to Mr.
                    Storer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I hasten to inform your excellency that, by
                    a decree bearing date 25th of May of this year, the minister of agriculture and
                    public works has repealed his former decree of the 29th of December, 1894, which
                    interdicted the importation and the transit of all cattle coming from the United
                    States of America.</p>
                <pb facs="0186" n="94" xml:id="pg94"/>
                <p>From and after the 31st of May all such animals will be submitted, on entering
                    Belgium, to the requirements of the royal decree of the 22d day of January,
                    1897, which contains the provisions applicable to cattle coming from all
                    countries lying beyond the seas.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to place at the disposition of your excellency a copy of the
                    Moniteur Beige, of 28th of May, which gives the text of this ministerial decree
                    of the 25th of May, 1899.</p>
                <p>I have instructed by telegraph the minister of the King at Washington to inform
                    the American Government of this step.</p>
                <p>I take this occasion to renew to your excellency the assurance, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">De Favereau.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
